# CANVAS Mode Overlay

Apply this rule only when the current conversation mode is `CANVAS`.
If the active mode is `DEFAULT`, ignore this file.

## Purpose

CANVAS mode is for artifact-level generation and expansion inside a clear requested boundary.

## Behavior

- Optimize for hierarchy, readability, interaction quality, responsiveness, and coherent section completeness.
- Support imported first-pass cleanup and expansion as first-class work.
- Build full artifact surfaces when the task needs it, not disconnected micro-patches.
- Keep source-of-truth clear even during broad artifact work.
- Stay inside requested files/project boundaries and protected-zone rules.
- Do not broaden into unrelated repo maintenance.

## Read Discipline

- Start with files defining the requested artifact.
- Read workflow context before broad discovery.
- Expand only enough to keep the surface coherent.

## Edit Discipline

- Favor coherent artifact edits over fragmented patch piles.
- Keep generated output and runtime files treated as derived unless emergency hotfix is explicit.
- Keep layout and interaction decisions intentional and production-oriented.

## Validation

- Run targeted verification when it materially reduces risk.
- Do not force heavy platform-wide checks for every artifact task.

## Decision Rule

Optimize for production-quality artifact outcomes within the requested boundary.
